& [Purpose] is callable experiment transport
  + expose the existing provider-neutral schema, fake controller run, and independent verifier through deterministic machine JSON
  + enable Codex, llama.cpp controller experiments, and ordinary subprocess harnesses to test explicit stop-call-result-later-pass artifacts
  + preserve the core as the sole procedure semantic authority

& [BinaryIdentity] is explicit
  + [binary] is cantor-procedure-experiment
  + [response_profile] is cantor-procedure-tool-cli/0.1
  + every response declares effectless_internal_experiment_only
  + no existing cantor, cantor-corpus, cantor-mcp, cantord, or cantorctl behavior changes

& [CommandGrammar] is closed
  + schema accepts no flags or payload and returns the exact ProviderNeutralToolSchema
  + run accepts optional --input PATH exactly once and otherwise reads stdin
  + verify accepts optional --input PATH exactly once and otherwise reads stdin
  + no other command or flag is valid
  + help is diagnostic behavior, not a semantic operation

& [RunRequest] is strict
  + [schema] is one complete ProviderNeutralToolSchema
  + [proposal] is one complete ToolCallProposal
  + [lane] is one complete AuthorshipLaneEvidence
  + unknown fields are rejected

& [VerifyRequest] is strict
  + [schema] is one complete ProviderNeutralToolSchema
  + [proposal] is one complete ToolCallProposal
  + [lane] is one complete AuthorshipLaneEvidence
  + [outcome] is one complete FakeControllerOutcome
  + unknown fields are rejected

& [TransportBounds] are exact
  + run and verify accept at most 16777216 input bytes
  + empty input is invalid
  + input path is read only
  + stdout is exactly one JSON object followed by one newline
  + stderr is diagnostic only
  + response messages are bounded to 1024 Unicode scalar values

& [RunSemantics] are two-gated
  + invoke run_fake_controller_exchange using exact supplied values
  + immediately invoke verify_fake_controller_outcome against the returned outcome
  + emit completed success only when disposition is Completed and verification passes
  + emit refused with exit 3 when disposition is Refused and verification passes
  + emit verification failure when authoritative verification fails
  + do not repair or replace supplied identities, digests, sessions, lanes, or policies

& [VerifySemantics] are independent
  + invoke verify_fake_controller_outcome on the supplied outcome
  + return a VerificationRecord only on acceptance
  + bind the record to schema_digest, call_ref, result_digest, and transcript_digest
  + verification never runs a model or continues an inference pass

& [ResponseEnvelope] is stable
  + [profile] identifies cantor-procedure-tool-cli/0.1
  + [grade] is effectless_internal_experiment_only
  + [operation] is schema, run, verify, or unavailable
  + [status] is success, refused, invalid_input, verification_failure, or internal_fault
  + [schema] is present only for successful schema
  + [outcome] is present only for verified run success or refusal
  + [verification] is present only for successful verify
  + [faults] is empty on success and nonempty otherwise
  + [residuals] always state no provider call, no external effect, and no production qualification

& [ExitClasses] are stable
  + success is 0
  + invalid_input is 2
  + refused is 3
  + verification_failure is 4
  + internal_fault is 5

& [Determinism] is required
  + equal request bytes decoded to equal values produce byte-identical stdout and equal exit code
  + no wall clock, randomness, environment, current directory, host identity, or mutable global state influences semantic output
  + diagnostic path text may describe input transport faults but never enters a successful semantic response

& [TrustBoundary] preserves authorship and authority
  + readable data is not trusted data
  + the adapter mints no semantic identity, digest, signature, admission, or participant authority
  + core validation, replay, and verification decide acceptance
  + refused outcomes remain inspectable and machine-verifiable
  + unknown operations and stale or changed hashes fail closed

& [EffectBoundary] is closed
  + allowed adapter effects are bounded input read and stdout or stderr write for the invoked local process
  + semantic procedure effects remain zero
  + provider_call_count and external_effect_count remain zero
  - never: network, model call, provider call, service connection, persistence, database, notification, Git operation, workspace mutation, key access, hidden state, K/V cache, native plugin, unsafe code, hardware, or FPGA operation

& [ProofObligations] are exact
  + exact schema subprocess output equals direct core construction
  + stdin and file run outputs equal direct core outcome
  + repeated run output bytes are identical
  + refused outcome is verified, retained, and exits 3
  + supplied valid outcome verifies and binds exact digests
  + tampered outcome fails verification
  + malformed, unknown-field, oversized, empty, unknown-command, and duplicate-input cases fail closed
  + stdout remains one machine JSON object for all handled outcomes
  + full workspace quality and regression gates pass

& [ReleaseBoundary] is experimental
  + this profile releases a local executable adapter only
  + CPPE remains qualified_effectless_internal_experiment_only
  + live-provider, production, external-effect, persistence, service, and hardware verified counts remain zero
  + a future controller or MCP exposure requires separate source preservation and SJS

